[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
cqrlog was installed

1) cqrlog settings are located at ~/.config/cqrlog directory

2) Log messages are stored to user folder database (~/.config/cqrlog/database),
   local MySQL/MariaDB server or external server.

3) If you want to use local or external MySQL/MariaDB server, don't forget add
   cqrlog user grants.

   CREATE USER IF NOT EXISTS 'cqrlog_user'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'cqrlog_pass';
   GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON *.* TO 'cqrlog_user'@'localhost';
   FLUSH PRIVILEGES;

   Change localhost by your server IP/hostname if it is a external networked
   SQL server

4) If you are running cqrlog with MySQL user folder database, disable MySQL X
   protocol uncomment a line from ~/.config/cqrlog/mysql.cnf file

   # MySQL X protocol
   mysqlx=OFF

   This change will take effect when cqrlog is restarted
EOM
}
]
